    "blurb": "The first time a model read a recipe off a website and executed it in a kitchen robot was RT-2 (Google DeepMind, July 2023). RT-2 discretized actions as text tokens, co-fine-tuned a VLM on web data plus robot-action data, and proved that web-scale vision-language knowledge transfers to robotic control. OpenVLA (June 2024) shipped the open 7B reference. Physical Intelligence's π0 series (2024-2025) added flow-matching action experts. NVIDIA's GR00T N1 (March 2025) delivered dual-system (System 1 / System 2) control for humanoid robots at scale. The VLA primitive — vision-language-action, a single model that sees, reads, and acts — is the bridge between this phase's understanding models and the autonomous systems in Phase 15.",
