    "n": 6,
    "title": "MCP Fundamentals — Primitives, Lifecycle, JSON-RPC Base",
    "blurb": "Every integration before MCP was a one-off. The Model Context Protocol, first shipped by Anthropic in November 2024 and now stewarded by the Linux Foundation's Agentic AI Foundation, standardizes discovery and invocation so any client can speak to any server. The 2025-11-25 spec names six primitives (three server, three client), a three-phase lifecycle, and a JSON-RPC 2.0 wire format. Learn those and the rest of the MCP chapter of this phase becomes reading.",
