    "blurb": "Most MCP tutorials show only stdio hello-worlds. A real server exposes tools plus resources plus prompts, handles capability negotiation, emits structured errors, and works the same across SDKs. This lesson builds a notes server end-to-end: stdlib stdio transport, JSON-RPC dispatch, the three server primitives, and a pure-function style that drops into either the Python SDK's FastMCP or the TypeScript SDK when you graduate.",
